WEBVTT

00:16.057 --> 00:17.142
It can't be.

00:17.434 --> 00:18.601
My sword...

02:15.051 --> 02:16.594
Incredible.

02:17.220 --> 02:18.638
He's totally out of our league.

02:18.721 --> 02:20.557
His sword is out of this world.

02:20.640 --> 02:22.559
He's simply poles apart from me.

02:22.892 --> 02:26.604
He even cut up a rock-hard fiend
as if he was slicing tofu.

02:26.771 --> 02:29.983
He's amazing!

02:31.484 --> 02:33.027
Who is he?

02:33.361 --> 02:35.780
I still have goosebumps!

02:44.998 --> 02:46.541
Hold it right there!

02:46.875 --> 02:49.002
I challenge you to a duel,
Mismatched Haori!

02:49.335 --> 02:51.838
You defeated
one of the Twelve Demon Moons.

02:51.963 --> 02:53.256
So I'm going to defeat you.

02:53.339 --> 02:54.757
That's what I've planned for.

02:54.841 --> 02:56.384
And then...

02:58.386 --> 03:01.055
I will be the strongest man around!

03:01.598 --> 03:04.267
Go back to your training, trouble seeker.

03:07.312 --> 03:08.605
What did you call me?

03:09.105 --> 03:11.733
The demon I just took care of
is not one of the Twelve Demon Moons.

03:11.858 --> 03:13.651
And you don't even know that?

03:13.943 --> 03:15.236
Of course I do!

03:15.361 --> 03:18.990
I didn't consider that small-timer one of
the Twelve Demon Moons to begin with.

03:19.282 --> 03:22.035
It's Tanjiro who said that
it was one of the Twelve Demon Moons.

03:22.118 --> 03:25.288
I was just going by what he said.

03:29.417 --> 03:31.377
What the hell? I'm tied up.

03:31.920 --> 03:33.004
He's fast.

03:33.129 --> 03:34.505
He moves really fast.

03:34.923 --> 03:36.799
Hey, hold it right there!

03:37.175 --> 03:39.886
You don't even realize
how bad your injuries are.

03:39.969 --> 03:41.512
You shouldn't have fought.

03:42.805 --> 03:43.890
I can't hear you!

03:43.973 --> 03:46.309
Your voice is too soft
and you walk too fast!

03:46.434 --> 03:49.812
I said hold it right there
and untie me now!

03:49.896 --> 03:51.481
Hey!

03:51.773 --> 03:55.193
Hey!

04:12.043 --> 04:13.962
Hello.

04:14.212 --> 04:15.880
Are you okay?

04:18.091 --> 04:19.592
Grandpa.

04:20.718 --> 04:22.762
Who's your grandpa?

04:23.554 --> 04:26.349
My grandpa dropped by.

04:27.308 --> 04:29.560
He told me not to give up.

04:30.478 --> 04:32.522
You saw your life flashing before you,
didn't you?

04:32.689 --> 04:36.985
It has been said that people see
flashbacks of life at the brink of death

04:37.360 --> 04:39.988
so they'll know how to avoid the fate

04:40.071 --> 04:43.866
from past experiences and memories.

04:44.909 --> 04:49.372
But well, I haven't experienced it,
so I don't know.

04:52.959 --> 04:56.087
You were smart to stop the poison inside
with your breath.

04:56.504 --> 05:00.675
If you hadn't done that,
you would've turned into a spider by now.

05:01.092 --> 05:02.927
Now I'm giving you the antidote.

05:06.139 --> 05:08.016
Hurry. Over here.

05:10.018 --> 05:11.060
Can you take them down?

05:11.602 --> 05:12.770
Be careful.

05:13.521 --> 05:15.398
It's okay. Everyone is still alive.

05:32.332 --> 05:33.916
My sword is broken.

05:34.584 --> 05:35.877
I can't believe it.

05:36.419 --> 05:38.212
Are this kid's threads

05:38.296 --> 05:42.258
tougher than the rock-hard demon
that I slashed before?

05:43.843 --> 05:45.928
I'm sorry, Master Urokodaki

05:46.471 --> 05:47.722
and Mr. Haganezuka.

05:48.306 --> 05:51.642
It's my lack of skills
that got my sword broken.

05:54.437 --> 05:56.647
No, this isn't the time for despair.

05:56.731 --> 05:58.441
Think!

06:00.276 --> 06:03.863
Since I can't cut the threads,
what if I go right for his head?

06:09.786 --> 06:10.912
That won't work.

06:11.120 --> 06:12.997
The threads seem to be alive.

06:13.081 --> 06:14.332
I can't just get past them.

06:14.540 --> 06:17.752
Besides, he's carefully manipulating
his threads not to kill me.

06:17.960 --> 06:19.670
Just so I can't do anything about it.

06:21.589 --> 06:22.507
Well?

06:22.965 --> 06:26.260
Don't you want to take back
what you just said?

06:29.097 --> 06:30.264
Very well.

06:30.556 --> 06:32.975
I'm going to tear you into shreds then.

06:34.852 --> 06:36.145
I can't dodge those!

06:47.240 --> 06:48.449
Nezuko!

06:52.537 --> 06:54.247
Nezuko!

06:54.580 --> 06:57.083
I'm sorry that you had to defend me.

06:57.875 --> 07:00.670
There's a girl in the box on his back.

07:01.129 --> 07:03.548
But she reeks of a demon.

07:08.678 --> 07:09.679
You...

07:10.430 --> 07:11.431
That...

07:12.890 --> 07:14.016
That girl...

07:15.184 --> 07:16.394
Are you two siblings?

07:16.894 --> 07:18.271
So what?

07:19.188 --> 07:20.606
The wound is so deep.

07:21.232 --> 07:23.359
Her left hand is almost severed.

07:25.570 --> 07:28.698
Please heal faster!

07:29.907 --> 07:32.201
Siblings...

07:32.827 --> 07:34.662
His sister is a demon.

07:35.121 --> 07:36.998
-And yet, she's still with him.
-Rui?

07:38.249 --> 07:41.711
His sister stepped out
to protect her brother.

07:42.920 --> 07:44.505
This is what I call a true bond.

07:44.839 --> 07:45.798
I want that!

07:46.174 --> 07:48.426
Wait... Wait a second!

07:48.885 --> 07:50.553
Please wait.

07:50.678 --> 07:52.180
I'm your older sister!

07:52.305 --> 07:53.723
Don't give me up like that!

07:53.806 --> 07:54.849
Shut up!

08:06.486 --> 08:10.573
In the end,
you failed to accomplish your missions.

08:11.157 --> 08:13.493
Each and every time.

08:14.327 --> 08:16.329
Wait.

08:16.579 --> 08:18.956
I'm your sister, right?

08:19.457 --> 08:21.042
Let me make it up to you.

08:21.501 --> 08:26.005
In that case, go finish off those people
wandering all over this mountain.

08:27.006 --> 08:30.384
If you can do that, I'll let you off
for what happened earlier.

08:32.053 --> 08:33.012
All right.

08:33.471 --> 08:34.805
I'll kill them all.

08:41.145 --> 08:42.188
Hey, kid.

08:43.481 --> 08:45.983
Kid, let's talk.

08:46.067 --> 08:47.109
Come out.

08:48.611 --> 08:49.695
Kid?

08:50.696 --> 08:51.739
Talk?

08:52.990 --> 08:55.743
I'm really touched.

08:56.536 --> 08:59.455
I can't help but shudder
at the bond between you two.

09:00.289 --> 09:04.043
I believe that no words can describe
what I'm feeling right now.

09:04.877 --> 09:07.713
But I still have to finish you two off.

09:08.589 --> 09:09.924
It's sad, isn't it?

09:10.091 --> 09:11.509
To face a tragic end like this.

09:14.804 --> 09:16.389
But there's only one...

09:17.265 --> 09:20.184
Only one way to avoid this horrible fate.

09:21.060 --> 09:22.895
Your sister...

09:24.188 --> 09:26.357
Hand over your sister to me.

09:26.941 --> 09:30.861
If you do that without putting a fight,
I'll let you live.

09:33.573 --> 09:35.950
I don't get what you mean.

09:37.159 --> 09:40.329
I want your sister to be my sister

09:40.746 --> 09:41.789
starting today.

09:42.957 --> 09:45.918
There's no way I'm going to agree to that.

09:46.460 --> 09:48.629
And Nezuko is not a commodity.

09:48.963 --> 09:51.048
She is conscious and can think on her own.

09:51.799 --> 09:54.260
She'll never become your sister.

09:55.469 --> 09:58.306
Relax, there's no need to worry.

09:58.806 --> 10:00.349
I'll create a bond between us.

10:00.975 --> 10:03.019
I'm stronger than you.

10:03.352 --> 10:05.146
I'm talking about the bond of terror.

10:05.605 --> 10:08.065
I'll teach her what happens
if she defies me.

10:08.274 --> 10:10.443
I've had enough of this crazy talk.

10:10.776 --> 10:13.154
You bind people using terror.

10:13.237 --> 10:15.072
That's not what a family bond is!

10:15.364 --> 10:18.326
If you can't figure out
where you went wrong about bonding,

10:18.492 --> 10:20.911
you won't get what you desire!

10:21.871 --> 10:23.456
You are so annoying.

10:23.581 --> 10:25.583
You don't have to scream.

10:26.000 --> 10:27.793
We both just don't see eye to eye, do we?

10:33.049 --> 10:35.676
I'll never give away Nezuko to you.

10:36.927 --> 10:38.304
That's fine with me.

10:38.554 --> 10:40.014
I'll take her once I kill you.

10:40.348 --> 10:42.767
I'll chop your head before that.

10:43.476 --> 10:45.478
What powerful words.

10:46.270 --> 10:48.272
Let's see if you can walk the talk.

10:49.899 --> 10:54.070
Let's see if you can beat me,
a member of the Twelve Demon Moons.

10:55.237 --> 10:56.322
Family.

10:58.324 --> 11:00.618
A father has a father's duties.

11:01.702 --> 11:04.205
A mother has a mother's duties.

11:05.706 --> 11:07.375
Parents protect their children.

11:08.542 --> 11:12.088
Older siblings
protect their younger siblings.

11:13.130 --> 11:14.507
No matter what.

11:15.925 --> 11:17.510
At the risk of their own lives.

11:18.761 --> 11:20.012
I believe that

11:20.554 --> 11:23.391
anyone who doesn't know their duties

11:23.766 --> 11:26.352
shouldn't exist.

11:27.812 --> 11:29.021
What about you?

11:29.814 --> 11:31.649
What's your duty?

11:33.067 --> 11:36.278
Your duty is to give up your sister
and get out of my sight.

11:36.987 --> 11:39.240
If you refuse, it's all over for you.

11:40.449 --> 11:41.826
Because you can't defeat me.

11:44.412 --> 11:45.955
Lower Moon Five.

11:46.997 --> 11:49.083
No wonder he's so powerful.

11:49.542 --> 11:51.919
He's a real Twelve Demon Moon.

11:53.003 --> 11:54.922
I can't cut his threads easily.

11:55.297 --> 11:58.217
What should I do with a broken blade?

11:58.884 --> 12:01.053
If his neck is tougher than his threads...

12:02.263 --> 12:04.014
What an irritating gaze.

12:04.181 --> 12:05.391
It's shimmering.

12:05.975 --> 12:07.351
You're such a fool.

12:07.810 --> 12:09.145
I don't suppose

12:09.603 --> 12:11.939
that you want to defeat me?

12:16.485 --> 12:17.445
Nezuko!

12:19.321 --> 12:21.574
I got her now.

12:21.991 --> 12:24.410
Do you realize what your duty is now?

12:24.577 --> 12:25.786
Let her go!

12:26.495 --> 12:30.499
I told you if you don't resist me,
I'll spare your life.

12:41.844 --> 12:43.179
Nezuko's gone.

12:51.228 --> 12:52.354
Nezuko!

12:59.862 --> 13:01.280
You're so noisy.

13:01.447 --> 13:04.992
Something like that won't kill her
because she's a demon.

13:06.035 --> 13:08.913
But now I need to teach her a good lesson.

13:09.413 --> 13:11.457
I'm going to let her bleed for a while.

13:12.416 --> 13:14.919
If she still doesn't cooperate,

13:15.085 --> 13:17.296
I'll leave her out here until daybreak

13:18.172 --> 13:19.715
and roast her a little bit.

13:20.090 --> 13:23.594
Let go of Nezuko!

13:46.367 --> 13:47.409
You...

13:47.493 --> 13:49.245
Do you actually think

13:50.538 --> 13:55.000
that you can chop my head off
just by getting close to me?

13:59.672 --> 14:02.299
Sure. Go ahead and chop me off.

14:10.432 --> 14:13.185
The sword couldn't cut him!

14:15.104 --> 14:16.021
Right?

14:16.146 --> 14:17.690
What did I tell you?

14:18.774 --> 14:21.068
You can't defeat me.

14:28.284 --> 14:32.288
My body is way tougher
than any thread I've manipulated.

14:33.205 --> 14:35.374
You can't even cut my thread.

14:35.457 --> 14:37.793
Let alone my neck.

14:49.096 --> 14:50.180
He's strong.

14:50.598 --> 14:54.268
His strength is way beyond any demon
I've encountered before.

14:54.852 --> 14:57.646
He's one of the Twelve Demon Moons.

14:58.814 --> 15:01.984
The power of a demon
closely related to Kibutsuji?

15:08.157 --> 15:09.283
Shut up.

15:09.658 --> 15:11.201
I need you to be quiet.

15:14.371 --> 15:15.748
Stop!

15:16.582 --> 15:18.876
I am your brother from now on.

15:19.251 --> 15:21.253
So stop whining.

15:24.006 --> 15:25.215
Calm down.

15:25.382 --> 15:27.134
Don't let anger get to you.

15:27.384 --> 15:29.637
You will only play right into his hands.

15:34.391 --> 15:35.726
She has lost consciousness.

15:36.894 --> 15:38.228
Is she sleeping?

15:39.396 --> 15:41.774
That's one unique demon.

15:42.024 --> 15:44.401
She's somehow different from us.

15:45.611 --> 15:46.695
Interesting.

15:48.030 --> 15:49.448
I must concentrate.

15:49.949 --> 15:54.620
Adjust my breath to unleash
the most precise, ultimate form.

15:55.204 --> 15:57.164
Total Concentration Breathing!

15:59.667 --> 16:02.252
Don't you realize
that you're only wasting your breath?

16:06.966 --> 16:08.425
Breath of Water.

16:08.717 --> 16:10.010
Tenth Form.

16:10.678 --> 16:12.638
Constant Flux!

16:17.935 --> 16:18.852
I did it.

16:18.936 --> 16:20.187
I cut the threads.

16:20.896 --> 16:23.607
His blade got more powerful
just by spinning.

16:24.441 --> 16:26.235
This is going to make things
a little harder.

16:27.069 --> 16:28.070
I did it.

16:28.237 --> 16:30.823
I just need to get closer
and I'll win this.

16:34.326 --> 16:35.285
Hey.

16:35.786 --> 16:38.914
Do you think this is the toughest
my threads can get?

16:39.915 --> 16:42.459
Blood Demon Art. Cruel String Prison.

16:44.128 --> 16:45.879
I've had enough of you.

16:46.296 --> 16:47.339
Now begone.

16:49.758 --> 16:50.801
Oh, no.

16:50.884 --> 16:52.302
I can't cut through these ones.

16:52.511 --> 16:54.054
My rotation isn't fast enough.

16:54.722 --> 16:57.141
And it smells totally different
from the other threads.

16:57.975 --> 17:00.436
And I can't lose!

17:01.311 --> 17:02.312
I'm going to die.

17:02.604 --> 17:03.522
I'm about to lose!

17:04.356 --> 17:05.441
I'm dead...

17:30.674 --> 17:31.800
Dad.

17:34.386 --> 17:35.512
Tanjiro.

17:36.680 --> 17:37.848
Breathe.

17:38.640 --> 17:40.142
Consolidate your breath.

17:40.601 --> 17:42.644
Be a God of Fire by all means.

17:52.863 --> 17:54.031
Tanjiro.

17:54.698 --> 17:55.741
Look.

17:55.949 --> 17:57.618
Your dad is performing the kagura dance.

17:58.744 --> 18:03.540
Our family works with fire
to protect us from injuries and disasters.

18:03.832 --> 18:08.796
During the New Year, we dance to
the God of Fire to pray for peace.

18:14.843 --> 18:16.345
Mom.

18:17.805 --> 18:20.015
Dad's body isn't very strong.

18:20.182 --> 18:24.103
Why is he dancing for so long
in the middle of the snow?

18:25.771 --> 18:29.149
Wouldn't that freeze his lungs?

18:32.277 --> 18:34.238
Because I have a certain way of breathing.

18:34.905 --> 18:38.325
To make sure that I don't get tired
no matter how tough it gets.

18:38.909 --> 18:39.993
Breathe?

18:40.786 --> 18:41.829
Yes.

18:42.121 --> 18:44.456
If you breathe right,

18:44.873 --> 18:47.167
you can keep on dancing
like me too, Tanjiro,

18:48.127 --> 18:50.212
without thinking of the cold.

18:51.630 --> 18:52.756
Tanjiro.

18:53.465 --> 18:56.385
Kagura and the earrings are our heirloom.

18:57.469 --> 18:59.847
They must be passed down
from generation to generation.

19:01.181 --> 19:02.683
This is our promise.

19:08.772 --> 19:10.274
Dance of the Fire God.

19:13.277 --> 19:14.486
Dance!

19:15.445 --> 19:16.446
My threads...

19:21.702 --> 19:22.703
Don't stop.

19:22.953 --> 19:24.163
Keep running.

19:24.663 --> 19:26.039
If I stop now,

19:26.165 --> 19:30.544
the Dance of the Fire God I created
from the Breath of Water will backfire.

19:31.295 --> 19:35.174
And if that happens,
I'll be paralyzed for a moment.

19:36.175 --> 19:39.094
So I must keep on running.

19:39.887 --> 19:43.056
I'm going for it! To protect Nezuko!

19:51.607 --> 19:52.608
He...

20:03.243 --> 20:05.370
I see it! The opening thread!

20:06.079 --> 20:07.873
I'm going to beat him here, right now.

20:08.165 --> 20:09.124
Even if...

20:10.167 --> 20:12.461
I'm going down with him...

20:14.838 --> 20:17.424
Nezuko.

20:19.134 --> 20:21.345
Wake up, Nezuko.

20:22.512 --> 20:24.139
Save your brother.

20:25.098 --> 20:27.017
I know you can do it now, Nezuko.

20:28.644 --> 20:29.686
Go for it.

20:37.027 --> 20:39.029
Please, Nezuko.

20:39.780 --> 20:42.157
Otherwise, your brother will die.

20:46.161 --> 20:47.663
Blood Demon Arts.

20:49.748 --> 20:50.958
Exploding Blood!

21:00.592 --> 21:01.593
Impossible!

21:01.843 --> 21:03.303
She burned off my threads!

21:04.179 --> 21:06.598
No one can break

21:07.182 --> 21:10.727
my bond with Nezuko!

22:54.164 --> 22:57.209
How did the Dance of the Fire God
cross my mind?

22:57.626 --> 22:58.835
Thank you, Dad.

23:00.128 --> 23:03.048
Thanks to him, my blade
can cut through the demon's neck.

23:03.131 --> 23:04.341
Thank you too, Nezuko.

23:05.217 --> 23:08.845
This week, I have a Taisho gossip
about the Kamado family.

23:08.929 --> 23:13.141
After the ritual, Mom and Dad
would make us some rice crackers.

23:14.476 --> 23:16.937
When we eat them,
they made loud cracking noises.

23:17.020 --> 23:18.230
Those were good times.

23:18.730 --> 23:19.940
Thank you, Nezuko.

23:20.023 --> 23:21.691
This is no time to relax.

23:22.943 --> 23:25.946
Next, episode 20, "Pretend Family."

23:26.029 --> 23:28.448
I've beaten one of
the Twelve Demon Moons, haven't I?

23:28.740 --> 23:30.325
TO BE CONTINUED

23:30.408 --> 23:31.993
Subtitle translation by CL Tan
